{
  "_comment": "Per-bone XYZ euler rotations in degrees on the MB-Lab rig. The rig's rest is a T-pose, so every pose states its own arms. Figure faces -Y. Measured on this rig: upperarm_L -Z / upperarm_R +Z brings the arm down to the side, upperarm X swings it forward, lowerarm Z is elbow flexion; thigh_* +X is hip flexion and calf_* -X is knee flexion. The renderer stands the figure on the floor itself, so no pose needs a root offset. upperarm Z past about -50 swings the hand inward as it descends rather than straight down, so arms-at-sides is not reachable on Z alone and 'stand' is an A-pose, as the \u00e9corch\u00e9 is. check-pose.py rejects anything that collides. A HINGE tips the pelvis forward and counter-rotates the thighs to keep the legs under it; measured, that counter-rotation has the SAME sign as the pelvis (pelvis +42 wants thigh +45), because the thigh's local X runs opposite to the pelvis's. Guessing the sign gives a figure lying flat in mid-air.",
